Is it necessarily an advantage for the Mines inhabitants to be
peaceful?  Gnomes are pretty easy to kill, and even dwarves aren't
_that_ tough.  As long as you can cope with them, they're an excellent
source of food, equipment, experience and weapon skills.

I think it would be a good idea to include some general discussion of
the merits and demerits of the different races before going on to the
list of which race is recommended to each class.  You might also want
to mention the good and bad points of the different alignments here
e.g. that Lawfuls can dip for Excalibur (most useful to Knights and
Valkyries) and chaotics suffer less penalty for murder, but there are
no useful chaotic artifacts except Stormbringer, which can be
dangerous.
